## Why This Is Asked
Tests cross-region, multi-tenant telemetry design with strict isolation, exactly-once semantics, configurable retention, and end-to-end observability under scale.

## Key Concepts
- Tenant-scoped partitioning and partition keys in Kinesis.
- Idempotent writes with per-tenant sequence tracking in DynamoDB.
- Late data handling and backfill strategy within 12 hours.
- Per-tenant retention, cost quotas, and audit trails.
- OpenTelemetry integration for end-to-end tracing across producers and consumers.

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo: guard against duplicate processing using a per-tenant sequence in DynamoDB
async function processEvent(event) {
  const tenant = event.tenantId;
  const seq = event.seq;
  const last = await dynamo.get({Key: {tenant}, ...});
  if (seq <= last.value) return; // duplicate or late
  await dynamo.put({Key: {tenant}, Value: seq});
  // write to downstream (S3, or Kinesis) atomically
}
```

